nodecode-handydandy is a rewrite of percyhendrux123-prog's percyhendrux123-prog/hermes-handydandy:

  https://github.com/percyhendrux123-prog/hermes-handydandy
  commit 3c085a5e21f312800ada2650db2a462462b5fa49
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Deploy Axiom (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's whole working part, in Common Lisp against Nodecode's
cell contract. Its three hooks (pre_api_request, transform_llm_output,
pre_llm_call) measured a Hermes session's size and appended a notice to the
answer or an instruction to the next request; here one :round hook reads the
turn's own meter -- the context the newest round filled against the model's
window, the input tokens, the rounds -- and records one line into the prompt
of the round about to be asked, plus one standing notice for the operator.
Its JSON state file and its file lock are gone: where a session stands is
that session's own state, which outlives a restart and needs no lock. Its
"connect" and "carryover" modes, already removed upstream, are not here; the
CSV of handoffs is kept as an optional setting. The handoff the plugin only
asked for in prose is now a tool, so the sections land in one file the cell
writes rather than wherever the model chooses.

Left out: the Hermes-only wiring (ctx.register_hook, plugin.yaml, the
HERMES_HOME and HANDYDANDY_* environment fallbacks), and the message-count
limit, which became a round limit because Nodecode's turn meter counts rounds
rather than messages. The plugin's own test suite is not carried over; the
cell has tests of its own under test/.
